Experiment 4
Title: To study and execute Linux process management commands and use Vi and Nano text editors for creating, editing and managing text files in Ubuntu Linux.  

Steps:
(A) Process Management Commands:
Open terminal in Ubuntu.  
Check running processes \rightarrow ps  
Display all running processes \rightarrow ps aux  
Continuously monitor processes \rightarrow top  
Find a process by name \rightarrow pgrep process-name  
Terminate a process \rightarrow kill PID  
Run a process in the background \rightarrow command &  
View background jobs \rightarrow jobs  


(B) Using Nano Editor:
Create/Open a file: nano test.txt  
Type some text.  
Press Ctrl + O \rightarrow Enter to save.  
Press Ctrl + X to exit.  


(C) Using Vi Editor:
Create/Open a file: vi test.txt  
Press i to enter insert mode.  
Type your text and press ESC.  
Type :wq and press Enter to save and exit.  


Result:
Successfully executed Linux process management commands and used Vi and Nano editors to create, edit, save and manage text files in Ubuntu Linux.


